  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the greatest integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Then the number of points in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> where the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msqrt></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous, is _____.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Now using the property of greatest integer function and&nbsp;simplifying the function we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>Now plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0034_b7742137fda9.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 223px;\" /></p><p>Now from the diagram we can say that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous at two points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>"
  }
